From a single worker:

```js
import worker from 'bare-translations'

const { modelId, modelType } = await worker.loadModel({ from: 'en', to: 'it' })

const { result } = await worker.translate({
  modelId,
  modelType,
  from: 'en',
  to: 'it',
  text: 'Hello world'
})

console.log(result) // 'Ciao mondo'

await worker.unloadModel({ modelId })
```

> [!note]
> Known issue in `qvac-sdk` with model not being fully shutdown. Tests will hang.

Manually instantiate one or multiple workers:

```js
import { WorkerClient } from 'bare-translations/client'

const worker = new WorkerClient()

const { modelId, modelType } = await worker.loadModel({ from: 'en', to: 'it' })

const { result } = await worker.translate({
  modelId,
  modelType,
  from: 'en',
  to: 'it',
  text: 'Hello world'
})

await worker.unloadModel({ modelId })
```

> NOTE: A worker spawns when an operation is requested and it stays running until the parent process is killed.

Terminate the worker:

```js
worker.close()

worker.onClose = () => {
  // worker terminated
}
```

Call the methods directly without a worker:

```js
import { loadModel, translate, unloadModel } from 'bare-translations/worker/translations.js'

const { modelId, modelType } = await loadModel({ from: 'en', to: 'it' })

const { result } = await translate({
  modelId,
  modelType,
  from: 'en',
  to: 'it',
  text: 'Hello world'
})

await unloadModel({ modelId })
```

